  "final_text": "**Proposed disposition:** ESCALATE, confidence 0.72. The case is C-A-261006-0015, awaiting a human decision. Level 2 would draft any STOR.\n\n**Three facts that drove it:**\n1. The trader placed one BUY limit of 27,326, which is 11.15 times average depth. It sat 2 ticks from the touch with nothing resting on the other side. The trader's typical order size is 500, and the desk is PROP with no registered market-making instruments.\n2. The trader sold 640 by market order 2.2 seconds after placing the BUY. The BUY order had no fills before that sale. It was hit for 4,707 only afterwards, and the remaining 22,619 was cancelled 704 ms after the sale. This is the \"caught in the book\" pattern in the escalation standard.\n3. The price moved 1.0 tick in the trader's favour, then reverted 1.5 ticks after the cancel. Cancel symmetry is 0.0, there were no market events and no risk events, and there is no parent order. None of the legitimate explanations is supported.\n\n**What would change my mind:** evidence that the BUY was a genuine client or parent order, or that the 640 SELL closed an existing position at a loss. A repeat of the cycle in the session would instead push it to DRAFT_STOR.",
